> = 0.02;

// The map is baked for the light on one side only; the other side reads it
// mirrored. That only works if the two halves of the face sit symmetrically
// in UV, which is worth checking rather than assuming -- on Hiro 82% of
// mirrored vertex pairs matched about u = 0.5, but a head laid out with the
// halves side by side instead of overlapping needs a different pivot, and one
// unwrapped asymmetrically needs the mirror off and a full bake.
